course: dictionary
lesson: 3724
title: Fling: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives fling three main meanings: to throw something hard, to move suddenly with force, and a short time of fun. The context tells you which one fits. «He flings the door open wide.» Here fling means moving the door quickly and with force.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «A salad spinner flings the water outward and off the leaves», the water is being thrown off, so fling means throw hard. Check by swapping in throw: «A salad spinner throws the water outward» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Fling can also be a noun, a thing that happens. A fling is a short time of fun, or a short love affair. In «the Highland fling», fling is part of a name for a Scottish dance, so the words around it tell you it is not about throwing at all.
fact: Fling is a verb: fling, flings, flung, flinging.
fact: To fling something means to throw it hard and carelessly.
fact: «Fling open» means to open suddenly and wide, as in «He flings the door open wide.»
fact: «Flung» is the past tense of fling, as in «a Mole flung down his spring-cleaning».
fact: A fling can be a noun: a short time of fun, or a short love affair. The Highland fling is a Scottish dance.
exercise: «The goblin shark can fling its jaws forward out of its face to grab prey.» What does fling mean here? | To sleep quietly | *To move suddenly and with force | To count slowly | To paint carefully
exercise: In «a Mole flung down his spring-cleaning», which form of fling is used? | flings | fling | flinging | *flung
exercise: In the phrase «the Highland fling», what kind of fling is it? | *A Scottish dance | A jump over a fence | A throw of a ball | A short love affair
test: In «He flings the door open wide», what does flings mean? | Knocks gently | *Pushes or throws open quickly | Paints | Closes slowly
test: What does a fling mean when it is a noun, as in «a short fling»? | A heavy stone | *A short time of fun | A school lesson | A bag of sand
exam: Which word in «A salad spinner flings the water outward» is the verb? | water | *flings | salad | outward
